    "field": "climate geoengineering",
    "problem": "Current mitigation efforts and future commitments are inadequate to accomplish the Paris Agreement temperature goals, prompting an evaluation of whether proposed climate geoengineering technologies can reliably address this shortfall given their substantial uncertainties, risks, and early stage of development.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a parametric analysis that compares projected CO\u2082 emissions with the remaining carbon budgets for the 1.5\u00b0C and 2\u00b0C goals to quantitatively assess the required scale of contribution from carbon dioxide removal or radiative forcing geoengineering techniques.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate proposed climate geoengineering techniques, including carbon dioxide removal and radiative forcing modification, to assess their potential contribution towards achieving the temperature goals set by the Paris Agreement.",
